            <ArticleTitle>[Pain assessment and interventional spine radiology].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1901-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Due to advances in interventional spine procedures, the radiologist can now participate in the clinical evaluation of patients. The purpose of this article is to review the main tools available to evaluate spine related pain and promote their use to demonstrate the efficacy of different interventional spine procedures.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
